{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Cross-Encoder Reranker Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`code/main.py` implements:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `CrossEncoder` - a small `torch.nn.Module`: token embedding, one transformer block with multi-head attention and feedforward, mean-pooled head producing one scalar."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `tokenize_pair(query, document)` - packs the two strings into a single id sequence with type ids that mark the boundary, deterministic and stdlib."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `train_tiny(pairs)` - one pass of supervised training on a hand-labeled (query, document, relevance) triple list, so the model produces sensible scores on the fixture."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `rerank(query, candidates, top_k)` - the production interface."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- `pipeline(query, retriever, top_n, top_k)` - the two-stage flow."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- A demo `main()` that loads the corpus from lesson 65's pattern, retrieves top-N, reranks to top-K, prints both lists side by side, and reports the latency of each stage."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run it:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```bash"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "python3 code/main.py"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The output shows the bi-encoder's top-N, the cross-encoder's top-K, and a timing summary. The cross-encoder takes longer per call but does not run on the full corpus. The two-stage total stays within the request budget while picking the answer that the bi-encoder ranked second or third."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Sweep N from 5 to 50 and plot recall@1 of the reranked output. Find the knee on this fixture.\n2. Train the cross-encoder for ten epochs instead of one. Measure the score-margin between positive and negative pairs at each epoch.\n3. Replace mean-pooling with a CLS-token head. Compare convergence on this fixture.\n4. Add a second cross-encoder head that predicts a binary \"is this answer in the document\" label. Use both heads at inference; one to rank, one to threshold.\n5. Replace the deterministic mock bi-encoder with the one from lesson 65 and chain the two stages. Measure the change in top-K versus bi-encoder alone."
      ]
    }
  ],
